    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** (65.99) and **Sam Antonacci** (64.49) serving as the focal points of our offensive engine. **Kyle Tucker** maintains our highest daily efficiency score, benefiting from a soft matchup against the lefty Ray, where he retains significant platoon neutral value. Meanwhile, **Sam Antonacci** earns a premier spot in the lineup thanks to his elite 0.391 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Lugo; his position as the leadoff hitter\u2014coupled with his ability to exploit the pitching profile\u2014makes him a high-floor asset for stolen base production, our most critical category. **Gunnar Henderson** (62.31) also projects for a strong outing, as the combination of a wind-aided environment and a favorable park factor offsets the challenge of facing a high-caliber arm like Fried.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involves the benching of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (48.73), who fell just shy of the lineup threshold despite his strong pedigree. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** offers high-end talent, he is currently suppressed by a tough matchup against Jax and a lower comparative efficiency score relative to our starting options. Elsewhere, we are leaning into aggressive play with **Nasim Nunez** (55.24) and **Coby Mayo** (57.16), both of whom are buoyed by park factors and wind-out conditions in their respective matchups. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the risks inherent in today's matchups. **Heliot Ramos** (42.73) faces a significant hurdle against Ohtani, resulting in our lowest projected start; his efficiency is hampered by the opposing pitcher's elite skill set, making him a high-risk play. Additionally, while we continue to navigate the absences of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** on the IL, the depth provided by **Brady House** remains on standby. Managers should keep a close eye on the official lineups for **Drake Baldwin** and **Liam Hicks**, as their projections are heavily dependent on confirmed order stability.",
